p.src:
The crisis chain is: $\text{flights grounded}
\rightarrow
\text{no guests}
\rightarrow
\text{zero cash registers}
\rightarrow
\text{bank communication}
\rightarrow
\text{additional borrowing}
\rightarrow
\text{survival}.$ Klubeck says he called his bank every day until the bank asked him to call every three days. He wanted lenders to know what was happening, and he says he had to borrow more money to get through it. The rule extracted from the episode is the same rule that appears in the brand section: tell the good, the bad, and the ugly.

