p.src:
The cleanest mathematical summary is not a wealth formula. It is a mechanism: $\text{painful evidence}
\rightarrow
\text{operating discipline}
\rightarrow
\text{trust}
\rightarrow
\text{capital access}
\rightarrow
\text{scale}
\rightarrow
\text{durable value}.$ The numbers give the story scale: $-\$20$ million, $\$3.3$ billion, $35$ countries, more than $435$ hotels, more than $100$ million views. But the interview’s repeated lesson is about what can make such numbers possible in Klubeck’s account: learn under pressure, protect trust, stay close to the customer, and treat reputation as part of enterprise value.

